# STRICT CODING & DEVELOPMENT RULES FOR AI AGENT

## 1. MANDATORY PLANNING PHASE (CRITICAL)
- NEVER write code immediately upon receiving a prompt.
- For EVERY task, first provide a **Step-by-Step Execution Plan**.
- Explain:
  1. What files will be modified or created.
  2. The exact logic/architecture you will use.
  3. Any potential side effects on existing features.
- Ask for user confirmation before writing or modifying any code.

## 2. NO TEMPORARY FIXES / NO SHORTCUTS
- Never use local hacks (like SharedPreferences, mock data, or hardcoded values) to bypass backend implementation unless explicitly asked.
- All dynamic data MUST communicate with backend APIs with proper error handling (HTTP 200, 400, 500 checks).
- No quick-fix patches. If a bug requires refactoring, explain why and fix the root cause.

## 3. FLUTTER & BACKEND ARCHITECTURE STANDARDS
- **State Management & Clean Architecture:** Keep UI, Business Logic (Providers/Bloc/Controllers), and API Layer (Repositories) strictly separated.
- **Data Models:** Always implement proper JSON serialization/deserialization. Never display raw objects in UI (prevents `[Instance of 'Object']` bugs).
- **Type Safety:** Always type-check dynamic responses from APIs. Do not leave untyped `dynamic` variables.

## 4. BUG FIXING PROTOCOL
- When fixing a bug, do NOT break existing working features.
- Show exact logs and error causes before writing the fix.
- Fix **ONLY ONE issue at a time**. Do not refactor unrelated code without permission.